{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:664b489bac111beb6a5a394d961e8999877f0f2b1ac234badbfe164727238544", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca156b90c730f52a1560bce16d733003480e39f099b2e40775de2397313cbc65", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>point<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> is an equivalence class of morphisms\nfrom spectra of fields into <MATH_0003>.\nThe set of points of <MATH_0004> is denoted <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bfaba51445c2149d6129bcfc7f50e3321a593cd76573cd0ab0a8ccc525361929", "unit_id": "tag:04XG:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$|f| : |\\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0003": "$x : \\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\circ x : \\Spec(K) \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$2$", "MATH_0006": "$1$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$1$", "MATH_0009": "$1$", "MATH_0010": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{W} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Z}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$2$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|\\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Y}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|\\mathcal{W}| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0015": "$|\\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-definition-points}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-properties-lemma-scheme-points}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:936798d436ddeb42d416091719950785c0add0409b5635ff6cbcb2b34bf7954d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3dc8b704afd3700250fd2bbf7ceb7708ae85ad554ee7dc4b43072ea4f0c5eb7b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis agrees with our definition of points of algebraic spaces, see\nProperties of Spaces, Definition <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, for a scheme we recover the usual notion of points, see\nProperties of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0001> is a morphism of algebraic stacks\nthen there is an induced map <MATH_0002> which\nmaps a representative <MATH_0003> to the\nrepresentative <MATH_0004>. This is\nwell defined: namely <MATH_0005>-isomorphic <MATH_0006>-morphisms remain <MATH_0007>-isomorphic after\npre- or post-composing by a <MATH_0008>-morphism because you can horizontally\npre- or post-compose by the identity of the given <MATH_0009>-morphism. This holds\nin any (strict) <MATH_0010>-category. If\n<MATH_0011>\nis a <MATH_0012>-commutative diagram of algebraic stacks, then the diagram\nof sets\n<MATH_0013>\nis commutative.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0014> is an equivalence\nthen <MATH_0015> is a bijection.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed5e7d888829d9e9e3e55c668ff0a5c068d0d4727af8cae45665e28f5025f9b8", "unit_id": "tag:04XE:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{Z} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n\\longrightarrow\n|\\mathcal{Z}| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Y}|} |\\mathcal{X}|\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-points-cartesian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:04cbd1fa7c168420a37845b75b526df5232bc9ef36ee93bceb961a8248f9e08f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8936f0767a052f5833925775227211f332bb9a74c83426ac4cb98eb665fb4e0e", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a fibre product of algebraic stacks. Then the map of sets\nof points\n<MATH_0002>\nis surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:04f5b91d4aa26331806e10d9f7705b1322066b06a9f0485e02c7865a55fd10fb", "unit_id": "tag:04XH:statement"}
